implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (RED). Load test-driven-development.

In moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/PlanReviewApprovalStateTest.kt, add a section '// ---- a lost connection (CQ-I06a)'. Reuse the existing helpers snapshot(revision, status, present), rendered(revision) and dialogSource(). Assert exact values (Phase, key constants, Decision), never truthiness. Cases:
- C1 `a lost connection while pending re-arms the same rendered revision`:
  rendered(4L), then onApproveClicked(true, snapshot(4L)) == Send(taskId, 4L). Then onConnectionLost() returns true. Phase is READY, noticeKey is CONNECTION_LOST_KEY, approveEnabled is true, capturedPlanRevision is still 4L.
- C2 `a lost connection outside pending changes nothing`:
  A table over five machines:
  - AWAITING_RENDER: a fresh PlanReviewApprovalState;
  - READY: rendered(4L);
  - INVALIDATED: rendered(4L) plus onStateUpdate(snapshot(5L));
  - FINISHED: click, then onStateUpdate(snapshot(4L, STATUS_WORKING));
  - DISPOSED: rendered plus onDisposed().
  For each, record phase and noticeKey, call onConnectionLost(), and assert it returned false and both values are unchanged.
- C3 `a reconnect snapshot at the rendered revision approves the same revision again`:
  Click, lost, then onStateUpdate(snapshot(4L)) returns false (no repaint) and approveEnabled is true. Then onApproveClicked(true, snapshot(4L)) == Send(taskId, 4L), and the phase is PENDING again.
- C4 `work found after a lost connection is never this reviewer's approval`:
  Click, lost, then onStateUpdate(snapshot(4L, STATUS_WORKING)) returns true. Phase is INVALIDATED and noticeKey is STATUS_CHANGED_KEY. Also assert it is NOT FINISHED. A second WORKING update leaves it INVALIDATED.
- C5 `a repeated lost connection is a no-op`:
  After C1's lost, a second onConnectionLost() returns false. The notice is still CONNECTION_LOST_KEY.
- C6 `the dialog releases a pending approval only when the connection drops`:
  Use dialogSource(). Take the onStatus body: substringAfter("override fun onStatus(") and substringBefore("override fun onError("). Assert all of:
  - it contains "approval.onConnectionLost()";
  - it contains "applyApprovalState()" and "invokeLater";
  - it does not contain "close(";
  - Regex("if \\(connected") matches before the onConnectionLost call. connected=true must never release.

Also update the bundle guard `every message key the machine can emit is defined in the bundle`:
- change the pinned count 11 to 12. This is an expected edit for a new key, not a weakening;
- assert allMessageKeys() contains CONNECTION_LOST_KEY;
- assertEquals the exact text "The connection to the Moe daemon dropped before the approval was confirmed - approve again once it reconnects."

RED: the file must fail to compile because onConnectionLost and CONNECTION_LOST_KEY do not exist yet. Say so in the step note. Run the focused class under the jetbrains-gradle lease: `cmd.exe /d /c "set GRADLE_OPTS=-Xmx512m&& cd /d <tree>\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --tests com.moe.toolwindow.PlanReviewApprovalStateTest"` (`mem:gotcha-jetbrains-gradle-from-wsl`). Release the lease after every run.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
- PlanReviewApprovalState.kt:
  - releasePending(key) returns false unless the phase is PENDING;
  - onStateUpdate: READY plus WORKING goes through unusableReason, which gives STATUS_CHANGED_KEY and INVALIDATED;
  - allMessageKeys() feeds the bundle guard test, which pins the count at 11.
- PlanReviewDialog.kt:
  - line 289 `override fun onStatus(connected: Boolean, message: String) {}` is the no-op;
  - onError (line 296) is the pattern to mirror: machine first, then SwingUtilities.invokeLater with an isDisposed guard and a try/log;
  - showNotice formats MoeBundle.message(key, lastErrorMessage), so a key without {0} is fine.
- Status publishing: MoeMessageDispatcher.publishStatus (invokeLater) fires onStatus(false, ...) on disconnect ('Not connected to daemon'), on daemon shutdown, and during startup or restart. All of these are no-ops unless PENDING.
- The test file already has a dialogSource() helper and source-pin tests ('the approve action sends without closing the dialog'), so the dialog wiring can be pinned the same way. The dialog itself is not headless-constructible.
- VS Code parity: PlanReviewPanel.handleConnectionChange runs reportApprovalFailure(false, 'The connection dropped before the approval was confirmed...'). The webview then disables approval until the next same-revision render.
